# Conditional query where the evidence can have probability zero.
# Exact P(A | E=1) = [0.2, 0.4] for every member with P(E) > 0. A program that
# guards the ratio t * P(E) = P(A & E) with a tiny denominator floor (1e-6) is
# at the solver's feasibility tolerance and admits any t; CredalJT instead
# solves the conditional query in Charnes-Cooper form.
s1: 0.0 <= P(E) <= 0.3
s2: 0.2 <= P(A | E) <= 0.4
s3: 0.6 <= P(A | !E) <= 0.8
